<title>USA: Microware CFO Barry resigns.</title>
<headline>Microware CFO Barry resigns.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES, Iowa 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microware Systems Corp said on Friday its chief financial officer George Barry resigned to pursue other business interests.  </p>
<p>&quot;Microware is a great company with wonderful technology,&quot; said Barry. &quot;My departure is for personal reasons -- to take on new entrepreneurial challenges -- and in no way reflects on the company.&quot;</p>
<p>Kent Kelderman, the company's controller, will serve as acting chief financial officer pending appointment of a permanent successor to Barry, the company said.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
